-- statement:
--   # Concrete surfaces, chart substitutions and lengths
--
--   This file sets up the local models used throughout the surface blow-up argument: power series
--   `k[[T,X]]` in two variables, the special fibers `k[[T,X]]/(T^a X^b)`, the concrete surfaces
--   `O[[T,X]]/(π - u T^a X^b)` over a discrete valuation ring `O`, the chart substitutions of the
--   blow-up, and the abstract `SurfaceData` with its state sets. It then proves the supporting
--   commutative algebra: ideals of `k[[T,X]]`, Gauss's count of irreducible polynomials over a finite
--   field, adic completeness of local rings and their quotients, and additivity of lengths of quotients.
--
--   ## Main results
--
--   * `card_pow_eq_sum_irreducible_degrees`, `irreducible_count_moebius`: counting irreducible
--     polynomials over a finite field.
--   * `axis_ideal_pow_mem_iff`, `axis_span_isPrime`: ideals generated by the variables of `k[[T,X]]`.
--   * `mvPowerSeries_fin_two_span_C_var_isPrime`: primality of `(c, X s)` in `A[[T,X]]`.
--   * `concrete_surface_contact_eq_special_fiber_contact`, `concrete_crossing_state_eq_union_cells`,
--     `concrete_single_state_eq_union_cells`: state sets of the concrete surface via the special fiber.
--   * `iInf_sup_pow_eq_of_isLocalRing`, `isAdicComplete_of_isAdicComplete_maximalIdeal`,
--     `isAdicComplete_quotient_of_iInf_sup_pow`: Krull intersection and adic completeness.
--   * `length_quotient_sup_mul_eq_add`, `length_quotient_sup_pow_eq_mul`: lengths of quotients.
--
--   Provenance: `Def_SurfaceBlowupV2_{LinearTowers, ResidueIdeals, ConcreteSurfaces, KillX,
--   SuccessorCharts, SurfaceData, TwoTermCokernels}` and the `Thm_SurfaceBlowupV2_*` nodes named after
--   the theorems of this file.

